# Component Structure

Every React component must live in its own folder. The folder name must match the component name.

```
ComponentName/
├── ComponentName.tsx
├── ComponentName.css
└── index.ts
```

## Rules

- Import components through their `index.ts` whenever possible.
- Never place `Component.tsx` directly inside the `components` or `pages` directories.
- Co-locate assets, hooks, tests, and helper files with the component they belong to.
- Page-specific components live in `src/pages/<Page>/components/` (see `04-project-structure.mdc`).
- When creating new components, always follow this structure automatically.
- When modifying existing code, preserve or migrate to this structure where practical.

## Example

```
src/components/ui/Button/
├── Button.tsx
├── Button.css
└── index.ts
```

```typescript
// index.ts
export { Button } from './Button';

// Consumer
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/Button';
```
